    "title": "Find the Smallest Divisor Given a Threshold",
    "category": "Binary Search",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer array nums and an integer threshold, choose a positive integer divisor such that the sum of ceil(nums[i] / divisor) over all elements is less than or equal to threshold. Return the smallest possible divisor.",
    "input": "Integer n Array nums Integer threshold",
    "output": "The smallest valid divisor.",
    "constraints": "1 <= n <= 5 \u00d7 10^4 1 <= nums[i] <= 10^6 n <= threshold <= 10^6"
